    "body": "## Summary\n\nFix several inconsistencies in bench serve result files:\n\n- Track pooling E2EL latency in the PyTorch benchmark export and record failed pooling requests.\n- Leave per-request arrays out of summary JSON and PyTorch export metadata.\n- Record the warmup count and use null for output-token metrics when the tokenizer is skipped.\n\nThis changes result serialization only; it does not change request execution or model output.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Ruff check and format on the changed Python files: passed.\n- Python compileall on the changed files: passed.\n- Focused serialization checks for exporter grouping, tokenizer-less metrics, and summary/detailed arrays: passed.\n- Full pytest was not run locally on macOS arm64; the checkout does not have the vLLM runtime and test dependencies installed. Regression tests are included for CI.\n\nNo model evaluation was needed because inference behavior is unchanged.\n\nFixes #58969. I checked the issue and open PRs before submitting. PR #55809 covers new server-side timing arrays, a separate change.\n\nAI assistance: OpenAI Codex helped implement and verify this change.\n",
